Since January not that much time has passed, but we all know how fast this market moves.

In just a few weeks the landscape can shift drastically.
$BTC went from ~90k to ~70k, the global macro environment is very uncertain, and the price action of $LIT has been disastrous.
All of this has clearly shifted sentiment around these projects.

In reality, pre-market valuations have dropped across the board, not just for perp DEXs but for many projects in general.

For example, @base moved from:
($6B) 65% → 29%

That said, points are still a decent incentive, especially in these market conditions.
And if we’re actually trading, not just farming points for the sake of it, then it’s basically an extra bonus.

At this point it probably makes more sense to use the platforms that offer the best trading experience and the best deal, rather than choosing solely based on points.

