@CCCNevada I have an update on my Mom's care.   Yes the administrators at CCCN, like most healthcare organizations and regulated industries, are very proud of their reams of policies and procedures.   

However, they have some incredible staff.  My Mom's doctor, Dr. Kingsley, made the decision after her first chemo to put her on the full dose at 85 because he thought she could tolerate it physically and I believe it saved her life.  On New Year's Eve my Mom got her labs done at 2:30 pm.  By 4 pm he had reviewed the labs and a prescription was waiting  for her at the pharmacy!  Where do you find attentiveness like that in healthcare anymore?!  She had a PET scan after her 4th chemo and she is in remission, almost nothing left of the cancer, she's ready to go back to Pilates and Mah Jong!!  So many of the nurses have been incredibly caring and wonderful.

The business of healthcare is a mess everywhere and especially here.  But I don't think she could have found better care anywhere.  I am profoundly grateful.

